en8811h: don't deref uninitialized fw buffer when firmware load fails

en8811h_read_fw() only sets *addr on success; on failure it returns the
error without touching the caller's pointer. u-boot's ubi_volume_read()
returns a POSITIVE errno (ENODEV=19) when the "en8811h-fw" UBI volume is
absent, so en8811h_load_firmware()'s `if (ret < 0)` check misses it: it
falls through and feeds the uninitialized `buffer` to air_write_buf(),
causing a Synchronous Abort + CPU reset during `Net:` init — before u-boot
reaches the prompt. An unprovisioned NAND can lack the en8811h-fw volume.

Init buffer = NULL and treat any non-zero ret as failure, so a missing/
unreadable firmware degrades to a clean "Load firmware fail." and u-boot
continues to boot (the PHY isn't needed for normal boot; the kernel loads
its own en8811h firmware). Path-agnostic: also fixes the FW_IN_MMC path.
Only compiled on boards with CONFIG_PHY_AIROHA_EN8811H (r3-mini, openwrt-one);
binary-neutral for r4/r3/r4-lite.

--- a/drivers/net/phy/air_en8811h.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/air_en8811h.c
@@ -550,11 +550,11 @@
 static int en8811h_load_firmware(struct phy_device *phydev)
 {
 	struct en8811h_priv *priv = phydev->priv;
-	void *buffer;
+	void *buffer = NULL;
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = en8811h_read_fw(&buffer);
-	if (ret < 0)
+	if (ret)
 		goto en8811h_load_firmware_out;
 
 	ret = air_buckpbus_reg_write(phydev, EN8811H_FW_CTRL_1,
